      "durationSeconds": 59.2,
      "transcript": "Lower town at Ruzika. From below, the fortress becomes heavy again by the water. In the lower town, turn around and look up. The same fortress that felt broad and almost walkable from above regains weight. Walls become higher, stone feels heavier, and the beautiful view turns back into mass, height, and descent. At Ruzika, the contrast is especially sharp. The quiet church sits inside military stone, with a story tied to an 18th century powder magazine later turned into a church. This corner keeps two memories together, defense and the human need for shelter, silence, and ritual. How high the upper walls now feel. Military stone beside a quiet church corner. The difference between panoramic fortress above and life below. This is a good place for a short rest on a quieter part of the route. After rain, the paths and descent feel heavier than they did above. Continue east toward the Riverside Tower, where the lower town reaches its most river-bound point.",
